  {
    "description": "Tool: "findContent"
Purpose:
Finds spaces, charts, dashboards, or Data Apps by name or description within a project, returning detailed information about each.

Usage tips:
- If results aren't relevant, retry with the full user query or more specific terms.
- A result carrying a \`<verified by="..." at="..." />\` element was approved by an organization or project admin as canonical, trustworthy content; \`by\` names who verified it and \`at\` says when. Verification is per item: a chart inside a verified dashboard is verified only when it carries its own \`<verified>\` element.
- A dashboard result previews at most its first 5 charts; use "readContent" to see all of them.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "definitions": {
        "__schema0": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "label": {
              "description": "The user's full request or its relevant part ("revenue based on campaigns", not just "campaigns"): the search understands natural language, so more context matches better.",
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "label",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
      },
      "properties": {
        "searchQueries": {
          "description": "Searches run together; pass several to cover different topics at once (e.g. "monthly revenue" and "user acquisition trends").",
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/__schema0",
          },
          "type": "array",
        },
        "spaceSlug": {
          "description": "Space slug or path to search only inside that space and its descendants, or null to search the whole project.",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null",
          ],
        },
        "verifiedOnly": {
          "description": "True searches only admin-verified charts and dashboards; spaces are omitted, and Data Apps stay included because they have no verification state. Verification is a status, not text, so search topic keywords rather than the word "verified". Null or false searches all content.",
          "type": [
            "boolean",
            "null",
          ],
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "searchQueries",
        "spaceSlug",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "findContent",
