    "description": "Open a pull request that adds the Lightdash preview-deploy GitHub Actions workflow to this project's repository: each pull request then gets a temporary preview project, torn down when it closes. Call it when the user asks to set up preview deploys ("deploy a preview project for each PR") or accepts your offer after getProjectInfo reports no preview-deploy workflow; no earlier writeback is needed. It automates GitHub Actions only; on other CI, tell the user preview deploys are set up by hand. It takes no arguments (the repository and dbt sub-folder are resolved server-side) and can take a few minutes.",
