  {
    "description": "Run one read-only bash command over a virtual filesystem of repositories: this project's dbt project at \`/dbt\` (its files at the top, e.g. \`/dbt/models\`, \`/dbt/dbt_project.yml\`) and every repository \`discoverRepos\` lists, whole on its default branch, at \`/<owner>/<repo>\`. \`ls /\` shows the mounts. Read repositories with this tool rather than asking the user to connect a GitHub MCP server. Use it to read the code before answering questions about it (a model's SQL, refs and lineage, project config, CI workflows), diagnosing a build or compile error, or proposing a change, and ground each claim in a file you read. Commands: \`ls\`, \`cat\`, \`head\`, \`tail\`, \`find\`, \`tree\`, \`wc\`, \`stat\`, \`grep\`/\`egrep\` (incl. \`-r\`, \`-l\`, \`-E\`, \`--include=GLOB\`), \`rg\`, \`sed\`, \`awk\`, \`cut\`, \`sort\`, \`uniq\`, \`tr\`, \`jq\`, \`diff\`, \`xargs\`, with pipes, \`&&\`/\`||\`, quoting, globs and \`2>/dev/null\`. \`search <term> [path]\` lists the files that contain a term, using the host's code search; the path picks one repository (\`/dbt\`, \`/owner/repo\`), a subdirectory, or every repository of an owner (\`/owner\`, one request each). It matches terms, not regular expressions, and indexes only default branches and files under a size cap: locate files with it, and use \`grep\`/\`rg\` for a regex, a non-default branch or matching lines in a known directory. Walks download what they touch (\`grep -r\` and \`rg\` every file, \`find\`, \`ls -R\` and \`tree\` every repository they enter), so one across repositories or over a whole large repository exhausts the provider's rate limit for the rest of the conversation, and the server stops a command that reads too many files. Keep walks inside one repository and directory, and find which files or repositories mention a string with \`search\`. Use as few commands as possible: locate files with one scoped command (e.g. \`find /dbt -name "*.yml" | xargs grep -l orders\`) and read them all with one \`cat a b c\`.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "command": {
          "description": "One read-only bash command, e.g. \`ls /\`, \`cat dbt_project.yml\`, or \`grep -rin "organization_events" /dbt/models | head -n 30\`.",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "target": {
          "description": "Starting directory as a repository "owner/repo" (e.g. "acme/analytics"), which starts the command in \`/owner/repo\`; null starts it in \`/dbt\`. Absolute paths reach any mount whatever the target, so one command can read named files from several repositories (e.g. \`diff /dbt/models/orders.sql /acme/analytics/models/orders.sql\`).",
          "type": [
            "string",
            "null",
          ],
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "command",
        "target",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "exploreRepo",
    "outputSchema": {
